#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:1
msgid "Release 0.7 (2005-01-12)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:3
msgid ""
"Binary patching. When upgrading components using pre-built binaries (through "
"nix-pull / nix-channel), Nix can automatically download and apply binary "
"patches to already installed components instead of full downloads. Patching "
"is “smart”: if there is a _sequence_ of patches to an installed component, "
"Nix will use it. Patches are currently generated automatically between "
"Nixpkgs (pre-)releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:10
msgid "Simplifications to the substitute mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:12
msgid "Nix-pull now stores downloaded manifests in `/nix/var/nix/manifests`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:15
msgid ""
"Metadata on files in the Nix store is canonicalised after builds: the last-"
"modified timestamp is set to 0 (00:00:00 1/1/1970), the mode is set to 0444 "
"or 0555 (readable and possibly executable by all; setuid/setgid bits are "
"dropped), and the group is set to the default. This ensures that the result "
"of a build and an installation through a substitute is the same; and that "
"timestamp dependencies are revealed."
msgstr ""
